    "answer": {
      "short": "No. His annuity will be worth $\\$8967.14$, leaving him $\\$1032.86$ below his target.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}n&=3\\times4=12\\\\r&=\\frac{10\\%}{4}=2.5\\%\\end{align*}$$\nFor 12 periods at 2.5% per period, the table factor is $13.7956$.\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\text{FV of }\\$1\\times\\text{regular payment}\\\\FV&=13.7956\\times650\\\\FV&=\\$8967.14\\\\\\text{Shortfall}&=10\\,000-8967.14\\\\\\text{Shortfall}&=\\$1032.86\\end{align*}$$\nGrant will not have enough for his trip; he will be $\\$1032.86$ below his target.",
